Pico SDK - From the Developer Command Prompt:
Navigate into the Pico directory you created to hold the pico tools
Clone the SDK: git clone https://github.com/raspberrypi/pico-sdk.git
Navigate into the sdk directory:  cd ~/pico-sdk
Update the submodule: git submodule update --init 
Add/ Update the PICO_SDK_PATH in the user environment

Install Picotool:
Refer to the Building instructions here: https://github.com/raspberrypi/picotool
Run this command from the pico-sdk directory: git submodule update --init lib/mbedtls
Install libUSB: https://github.com/libusb/libusb
Download this file: https://github.com/libusb/libusb/releases/download/v1.0.27/libusb-1.0.27.7z
Using 7zip, extract it into the tools directory
Add/ Update LIBUSB_ROOT path in the user environment
Download Picotool: https://github.com/raspberrypi/picotool/archive/refs/heads/master.zip
Extract picotool into a directory and create a build folder
 Using Developer Command Prompt, navigate into that build folder
 Execute: cmake -DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=<YOUR_INSTALL_DIR>          -DPICOTOOL_FLAT_INSTALL=1 ..
Execute: cmake --build . 
Execute: cmake –install .
Install USB Driver: https://zadig.akeo.ie/
         Download this file: https://github.com/pbatard/libwdi/releases/download/v1.5.1/zadig-2.9.exe
Execute Zadig and Install the driver
Add/ Update the user path to picotool

Doom Source files: https://github.com/kilograham/rp2040-doom
Download this file: https://github.com/kilograham/rp2040-doom/archive/refs/heads/rp2.zip

Installing SDL2 dependencies: https://github.com/libsdl-org/SDL
Download this file for SDL2 devel: https://github.com/libsdl-org/SDL/releases/download/release-2.30.10/SDL2-devel-2.30.10-mingw.zip
Extract and navigate into the “x86_64-w64-mingw32” folder inside SDL2-devel; add address to user path
Add the user paths for the SDL2 “include” and “lib” directories 
SDL2-mixer: https://github.com/libsdl-org/SDL_mixer
Download this file: https://github.com/libsdl-org/SDL_mixer/releases/download/release-2.8.0/SDL2_mixer-devel-2.8.0-mingw.zip
From 7zip, extract SDL_mixer into the SDL2-devel “include” directory
From 7zip, extract the 3 lib files into the SDL2-devel “lib” directory
SDL2-net: https://github.com/libsdl-org/SDL_net
Download this file: https://github.com/libsdl-org/SDL_net/releases/download/release-2.2.0/SDL2_net-devel-2.2.0-mingw.zip
From 7zip, extract the 3 lib files into the SDL2-devel “lib” directory
From 7zip, extract SDL_mixer into the SDL2-devel “include” directory

Building Doom for RP2350:
Navigate into RP2350 arm build directory, insure it is empty.
Execute:
cmake -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=MinSizeRel -DPICO_BOARD=vgaboard -DPICO_SDK_PATH=<path to your pico sdk> -DPICO_PLATFORM=rp2350-arm-s -Dpicotool_DIR=<path to your picotool> -DPICO_EXTRAS_PATH=<path to your pico_extras> -G "NMake Makefiles" ..
Execute: nmake
Put the Pico 2 into Boolsel mode and install game engine by dragging “doom_tiny_usb.uf2” from the “src” directory of build directory into the Pico 2.
Unplug and reconnect the Pico 2 in Bootsel mode
Navigate into the root directory of Doom (where doom1.whx is)
Execute: picotool load -v -t bin doom1.whx -o 0x10042000.
Unplug the Pico 2 and plug it into a powered USB hub with keyboard attached

Building RP2350 RISC-V binary:
From inside the risc-v build directory, execute: cmake -DPICO_PLATFORM=rp2350-riscv -Dpicotool_DIR=F:\Users\tools\picotool -DPICO_EXTRAS_PATH=F:\Users\pico2\pico-extras-master -DPICO_TOOLCHAIN_PATH=F:\Users\tools\bin -G “NMake Makefiles” ..
nmake
